        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "An industrial packaging manufacturer entered into a written contract with an agricultural cooperative to produce and deliver 100,000 heavy-duty polypropylene grain sacks for $80,000, with delivery on August 1. The contract contained the following clause: 'No assignment of rights or delegation of performance under this contract shall be made by either party without the prior written consent of the other; any assignment without consent shall be void.' On July 25, the manufacturer completed manufacturing all 100,000 sacks in full conformity with specifications and delivered them to the cooperative's warehouse. The cooperative inspected and accepted the sacks on July 28. On July 29, the manufacturer executed a written assignment to a commercial factoring company: 'Manufacturer assigns to Factoring Co. all of its rights to receive the $80,000 payment due from Cooperative on August 1.' The factoring company paid the manufacturer $72,000 cash for the account and immediately served formal written notice of the assignment on the cooperative. The cooperative refused to pay the factoring company on August 1, citing the contract's express anti-assignment clause containing voidness language.",
