            "No, because an assignee of an account stands in the shoes of the assignor and is subject to all express contractual restrictions agreed to by the assignor.",
            "Yes, because under UCC § 2-210(2) and § 9-406, a contractual term prohibiting the assignment of an account or right to payment for goods fully delivered is legally ineffective.",
            "Yes, but only if the factoring company proves that the cooperative acted in bad faith in refusing to consent."
