        fp: "Defendant and an accomplice agreed to break into an unoccupied dwelling house at night to steal firearms. When they reached the house, the accomplice broke a basement window with a rock, and both men climbed inside. While searching the living room, the accomplice used an iron pry bar to force open a locked gun cabinet. An armed neighbor who lived nearby heard breaking glass, walked over with a rifle, and observed the two men inside through an open window. The neighbor pointed the rifle through the window and shouted, 'Freeze, police!' The accomplice turned toward the window and raised the iron pry bar in a threatening manner. Believing the accomplice was about to attack, the neighbor fired a shot in lawful self-defense, striking the accomplice in the chest and killing him instantly. Defendant immediately dropped to the floor and surrendered. The jurisdiction follows the common law 'agency theory' of felony murder.",
