            "Yes, because under Restatement (Second) of Contracts § 89, a modification of an executory contract is binding if it is fair and equitable in view of circumstances not anticipated by the parties when the contract was made.",
            "No, because the contractor's threat to walk off the job constituted economic duress as a matter of law.",
            "Yes, because under UCC § 2-209, modifications made in writing between commercial entities require no consideration to be binding."
